config DNS_OPTIMIZER
	tristate "DNS A/AAAA race answer and fast retransmit"
	depends on INET && IPV6 && NETFILTER && NF_CONNTRACK
	help
	  Netfilter hooks that shorten DNS stalls for apps:

	  - race: when an app asked for A and AAAA and only one family got
	    an address, the other query is answered with an empty NOERROR
	    once it times out, so the app goes on with what it has.
	  - fast retransmit: an unanswered A/AAAA query is re-sent after
	    min(8 * measured DNS RTT, 2 s) instead of waiting for the
	    resolver's own timeout.

	  Both are switched in /proc/sys/net/dns_optimizer/.

	  If unsure, say N.
